From ba542b29b03e1ef822f250dc885c09e622eeadb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:35:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/60] virtio-balloon: free page reporting, with discard on
 Windows

P3.5 dynamic memory, level 1: let the host working set follow what the
guest actually uses. Guest RAM stays committed (private bytes do not
change); what goes back to Windows is the physical memory behind pages
the guest reports as free.

virtio-balloon gets VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_REPORTING and
VIRTIO_BALLOON_F_PAGE_POISON from upstream QEMU 5.1 (91b867191ddf
"virtio-balloon: Provide an interface for free page reporting",
7483cbbaf820 "virtio-balloon: Implement support for page poison reporting
feature"), adapted to this tree: qemu_balloon_is_inhibited() instead of
virtio_balloon_inhibited(), no free page hinting, and a config space that
stays 8 bytes unless page-poison is on. New properties as upstream:
free-page-reporting (default off) and page-poison (default on). Reported
blocks go to ram_block_discard_range(). The device logs one line per GiB
discarded.

ram_block_discard_range() had no Windows path (QEMU_MADV_DONTNEED is
invalid there). It now calls the new qemu_win32_discard_memory(), which
uses DiscardVirtualMemory and falls back to MEM_RESET + VirtualUnlock.
File-backed (Quick Boot ram.img), user-backed and preallocated blocks
are skipped with a one-time warning.

Measured on this host (Windows 11 26200) with a standalone WHP partition
(C:\emu-src\work\balloon\whpprobe): after the guest filled 256 MiB that
is mapped with WHvMapGpaRange, DiscardVirtualMemory dropped all 65536
pages from the working set (262 -> 6 MiB, system available +246 MiB),
private bytes stayed 259 MiB, guest and host then saw the same zeroed
pages and each other's later writes (0 mismatches). MEM_RESET alone freed
nothing; MEM_RESET + VirtualUnlock freed the working set but kept the
old contents. DiscardVirtualMemory costs about 0.8 ms per 4 MiB.

Enable with: -qemu -device virtio-balloon-pci,free-page-reporting=on

Change-Id: I2b35d4614ab686beb448defe0a2e205857022040
